maria: Heads-up — opened PR to add practical examples for function/tool calling + structured-output (JSON Schema guardrails + parsing pattern examples). PR: https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/912 (draft). Need a quick QA pass from docs + devex.
josh: thanks! is this covering both python/js SDK snippets and the Responses vs Completions differences?
anya: yup, plan is to show both SDKs + a small migration note about schema strictness (old responses can omit optional keys). also include an example for null fields and type unions.
sam: can you drop a minimal example here so i can sanity-check parsing in the parser tests?
maria: sure — minimal response payload we expect from the model when schema enforces a restaurant suggestion:```json
{
  "type": "restaurant_suggestion",
  "name": "Taco House",
  "rating": 4.5,
  "address": null
}
```
anya: and the schema we're using in the docs (small, explicit about nulls):```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "type": {"const": "restaurant_suggestion"},
    "name": {"type": "string"},
    "rating": {"type": ["number", "null"]},
    "address": {"type": ["string", "null"]}
  },
  "required": ["type", "name"]
}
```
josh: perfect. can we include SDK snippets that show enforcing schema + fallback parsing? like show how to handle when model returns plain text instead of JSON.
maria: added two patterns: optimistic parse (try json.loads) and guarded parse (use a regex to extract JSON block first). example in python:```python
# optimistic
try:
    out = json.loads(resp.text)
except ValueError:
    # fallback: extract first {...} block
    m = re.search(r"\{.*\}", resp.text, re.S)
    out = json.loads(m.group(0)) if m else { }
```
and JS:```javascript
// optimistic
try {
  const out = JSON.parse(text);
} catch(e) {
  const m = text.match(/\{[\s\S]*\}/);
  const out = m ? JSON.parse(m[0]) : {};
}
```
anya: also propose a short migration note under "Behavior changes" — when adding schema validation to older prompts, customers may see more truncated/null values; recommend staged rollout + a test prompt set.
sam: for tests: i can add a small jsonl fixtures file with 6 edge cases (missing field, null, extra field, nested array, wrong type as string, text + JSON). i'll wire it to docs CI.
maria: great — also need link fixes: a few links in the callouts point at old internal RFCs. i've replaced them in the draft but ask docs review to sanity check.
